OL,3,GNEWSAMP urges action on illegal waste
OL,4,Asite in Dorking
OL,5,
OL,6,FAn MP has urged the Environment Agency
OL,7,F(EA) and two Surrey councils to use
OL,8,Ftheir powers to clear an unauthorised
OL,9,Fwaste site, after a final deadline
OL,10,Fpassed on 3 September.
OL,12,FSurrey County Council (SCC) issued an
OL,13,Fenforcement notice over the land at
OL,14,FDorking West Station Yard in May, but
OL,15,Fthere is currently still rubbish on the
OL,16,Fsite.
OL,18,FDorking and Horley's Liberal Democrat
OL,19,FMP Chris Coghlan said it was "deeply
OL,20,Ffrustrating" that more progress had not
OL,21,Fbeen made.
OL,23,APub: 21-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,328,320,200,140,0,100
